Loom: a concat result may share registers with an already placed concat or slice result when every shared unit holds
the same producer's unit (followed back through concat and slice relations) and neither value is written in place
before the other dies. Before, two views built from the same loads (an AIE2P accumulator quad used whole and as two
halves) counted as conflicting values, so allocation failed or copied. Byte-identical on every set the engine emits
(pp2048, 128K context, native, decode, native with the NPU split); the Scratch NPU attention kernel needs it to load
each S block once (with the CSE and concat reservation changes, not yet patches).
diff --git a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/coalescing.c b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/coalescing.c
index 1e8a5da038..d436ebe673 100644
--- a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/coalescing.c
+++ b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/coalescing.c
@@ -821,6 +821,172 @@ loom_low_allocation_coalescing_assign_edge_destination_interval(
       context, interval, relation, out_assigned);
